#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" :question/math-academy-id "e-3065" :question/problem "Consider the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1 ,\\: 8t+2 ,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t.$ Find $\\mathbf R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since  $s=6\\sqrt{2}t,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2}t & =s \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s \\geq 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})-1,\\,8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})+2,\\,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}-1,\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6}+2,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s-6,\\,4\\sqrt{2}s+12,\\,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3066" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2t|\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0.$ \n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{s} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0.$  \n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,i+2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3067" :question/problem "Given the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t,$ we have that $t=\\dfrac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s,$ the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1fe70b-f9e8-5e14-95bd-936e4e6cefc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260006} {:answer/id #uuid "174557aa-b7d9-5229-9f98-28ccb93a8901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260078} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8c4418-1037-56d1-b0a9-ef14f6a55e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260275} {:answer/id #uuid "76f3812d-d66e-52ea-96bd-1ff609fa35c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260914} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d052fe-6c22-51b8-9ad5-eac40c0785c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c8c4418-1037-56d1-b0a9-ef14f6a55e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260275} :answer-field/id #uuid "d38f3ab6-9be0-5e12-942e-e5d33286db0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10934b16-caa8-5843-93a5-554278b82678" :question/math-academy-id "q-127687" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={e}^{t}-1.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have that $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc36f85-1102-5b80-a094-c10071f3364c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨2s,\\,3s,\\,2-\\sqrt{3}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260408} {:answer/id #uuid "9e30404b-905a-57cd-82cf-234f22d1abc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s-3,\\,-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261246} {:answer/id #uuid "ad627246-dce6-5769-8332-676206ded725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨3s,\\,s,\\,1-\\sqrt{6}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261393} {:answer/id #uuid "bb67c9f7-2efa-5489-a1d0-6cdfde17faa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s+3,\\,2s-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261525} {:answer/id #uuid "fa040405-81a8-51bd-8162-855fbd609651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa040405-81a8-51bd-8162-855fbd609651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262058} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a4d7171-4466-5034-b27a-ebb267da9c78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35d19d31-9377-5a1f-a9f6-e8ea15486111" :question/math-academy-id "q-127739" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2,\\,3-{t}^{4}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2{t}^{3}|\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}\\sqrt{4+1+4} \\\\  & =6{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}6{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{t}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}$ and $t\\ge 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ {t}^{4} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}+2,\\,3-{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3},\\,\\frac{s}{3}+2,\\,3-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e527b9-3209-50d5-aaa3-8bf133b7f3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,1-3s,\\,5+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312004} {:answer/id #uuid "860b9d1d-8a3f-5f6e-aa07-757fcfca11c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313051} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb65002-7c68-5ed0-bc75-f31eba7bc763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313215} {:answer/id #uuid "9efdae8e-52ac-5d4d-910f-4cc2786f8b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313225} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1543e9-0a7e-55d3-8cb0-c7b5bb91f9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb1543e9-0a7e-55d3-8cb0-c7b5bb91f9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e94e688-21a1-5bc1-bdf8-2b812cd1d886" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd2d22fe-d6c9-55e5-8f32-f782e37e2d9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33860" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,1-3t,\\,5+6t⟩$, $t\\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,1-3(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,5+6(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9354c249-a806-5aee-8b9e-c2cab0e55bb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨3s, 2\\sin (2s), 2\\cos (2s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117862} {:answer/id #uuid "c886eba5-d614-5e34-8485-3765c24384e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨3s, 2\\sin (5s), 2\\cos (5s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117863} {:answer/id #uuid "e27db88c-91f0-5321-8ab9-db1460ca7af1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨\\frac{3s}{5}, 2\\sin (\\frac{2s}{5}), 2\\cos (\\frac{2s}{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117864} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd71891-e2fe-55be-b7d2-c89be261b9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨\\frac{3s}{10}, 2\\sin (\\frac{s}{5}), 2\\cos (\\frac{s}{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117865} {:answer/id #uuid "48a0f963-6a75-5bf8-8930-64b6711bb277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨3s\\sqrt{5}, 